#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr "Terminología"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "The specifications use a handful of classifications over and over. Learn these and the rest of the blueprint reads easily. Every other term is in the [glossary]{1} or in the vocabulary of its bounded context, listed in the [context map]{2}."
msgstr "Las especificaciones usan una y otra vez un puñado de clasificaciones. Apréndalas y el resto del plano se leerá con facilidad. Todos los demás términos están en el [glosario]{1} o en el vocabulario de su contexto delimitado, enumerado en el [mapa de contextos]{2}."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Sensitivity tiers"
msgstr "Niveles de sensibilidad"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Every table is tagged with one tier. The tier decides who may see it, where it is stored and whether it may be published."
msgstr "Cada tabla lleva un nivel. El nivel decide quién puede verla, dónde se almacena y si se puede publicar."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Tier"
msgstr "Nivel"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Nombre"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "EMIS example"
msgstr "Ejemplo en un SIGE"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "In short"
msgstr "En resumen"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "T0"
msgstr "T0"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Public aggregate"
msgstr "Agregado público"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Enrolment by district, published"
msgstr "Matrícula por distrito, publicada"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Anyone may see it"
msgstr "Cualquiera puede verlo"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "T1"
msgstr "T1"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Internal"
msgstr "Interno"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "The list of institutions and their facilities"
msgstr "La lista de instituciones y sus instalaciones"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Staff of the authority"
msgstr "El personal de la autoridad"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "T2"
msgstr "T2"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "De-identified"
msgstr "Desidentificado"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Learner records with names removed and identifiers replaced"
msgstr "Registros de estudiantes sin nombres y con identificadores sustituidos"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Approved analysts and partners"
msgstr "Analistas y socios aprobados"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "T3"
msgstr "T3"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Identifiable"
msgstr "Identificable"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "A learner's name, birth date and enrolment"
msgstr "El nombre, la fecha de nacimiento y la matrícula de un estudiante"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Only those with a need and the right scope"
msgstr "Solo quienes lo necesitan y tienen el ámbito adecuado"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "T4"
msgstr "T4"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Special category"
msgstr "Categoría especial"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Health, disability, child-protection records"
msgstr "Salud, discapacidad, expedientes de protección de la infancia"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Named people, each grant approved by a steward, in separate storage"
msgstr "Personas con nombre, cada permiso aprobado por una persona responsable de datos, en almacenamiento separado"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Defined in [CAP-CLASSIFICATION]{1}."
msgstr "Definido en [CAP-CLASSIFICATION]{1}."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Provenance"
msgstr "Procedencia"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Every table also says where its data came from: **real** (about real people and institutions), **simulated** (made up, for testing) or **derived** (computed from other tables). Nothing is deleted until its provenance is proven."
msgstr "Cada tabla indica también de dónde vienen sus datos: **real** (sobre personas e instituciones reales), **simulated** (inventados, para pruebas) o **derived** (calculados a partir de otras tablas). No se borra nada hasta que se demuestra su procedencia."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Bronze, silver and gold"
msgstr "Bronce, plata y oro"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Data passes through three stages on its way to being used:"
msgstr "Los datos pasan por tres etapas antes de usarse:"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Stage"
msgstr "Etapa"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Holds"
msgstr "Contiene"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Ejemplo"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Bronze"
msgstr "Bronce"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Data exactly as received"
msgstr "Los datos exactamente como se recibieron"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "A census return file, unchanged"
msgstr "Un archivo de declaración del censo, sin cambios"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Silver"
msgstr "Plata"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Data checked and made consistent"
msgstr "Los datos comprobados y hechos coherentes"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Returns with codes validated and institutions matched to the registry"
msgstr "Declaraciones con códigos validados e instituciones vinculadas al registro"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Gold"
msgstr "Oro"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Data ready to use"
msgstr "Los datos listos para usar"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Enrolment counts by grade and district, as at census day"
msgstr "La matrícula por grado y distrito, en el día del censo"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Reports and indicators read only from gold."
msgstr "Los informes y los indicadores leen solo de la capa oro."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Reference date and academic period"
msgstr "Fecha de referencia y periodo académico"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "An **academic period** is a school year or term."
msgstr "Un **periodo académico** es un curso escolar o un trimestre."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "A **reference date** is the single day a statistic describes, such as census day. Counting \"as at\" one date is what makes figures comparable."
msgstr "Una **fecha de referencia** es el único día que describe una estadística, como el día del censo. Contar «a» una sola fecha es lo que hace comparables las cifras."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Layers"
msgstr "Capas"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "The platform is built in four layers, each trusted less than the one below and each in its own repository."
msgstr "La plataforma se construye en cuatro capas, cada una con menos confianza que la de abajo y cada una en su propio repositorio."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Layer"
msgstr "Capa"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "L0"
msgstr "L0"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Bootstrap"
msgstr "Arranque"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "The root of trust, made once by a person"
msgstr "La raíz de confianza, creada una vez por una persona"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "L1"
msgstr "L1"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Platform"
msgstr "Plataforma"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Shared storage, compute, catalog, identity and governance"
msgstr "Almacenamiento, cómputo, catálogo, identidad y gobernanza compartidos"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "L2"
msgstr "L2"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Modules"
msgstr "Módulos"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Reusable building blocks"
msgstr "Piezas reutilizables"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "L3"
msgstr "L3"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Products"
msgstr "Productos"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Workloads such as a census or document review"
msgstr "Cargas de trabajo como un censo o la revisión de documentos"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Capabilities, clauses and bindings"
msgstr "Capacidades, cláusulas y vinculaciones"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "A **capability** is something the platform must be able to do, such as `CAP-ACCESS`."
msgstr "Una **capacidad** es algo que la plataforma debe poder hacer, como `CAP-ACCESS`."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Its **contract** is a list of numbered **clauses**, such as `CAP-ACCESS.7`. Each clause has a level: **MUST** (required), **SHOULD** (required unless there is a recorded reason) or **MAY** (optional), in the sense of [BCP 14]{1}. Each says how conformance is shown."
msgstr "Su **contrato** es una lista de **cláusulas** numeradas, como `CAP-ACCESS.7`. Cada cláusula tiene un nivel: **MUST** (obligatorio), **SHOULD** (obligatorio salvo razón registrada) o **MAY** (opcional), en el sentido de [BCP 14]{1}. Cada una indica cómo se demuestra la conformidad."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "An **implementation** is a real platform that meets the contracts. Its **binding** gives every clause a status:"
msgstr "Una **implementación** es una plataforma real que cumple los contratos. Su **vinculación** da un estado a cada cláusula:"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Status"
msgstr "Estado"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Means"
msgstr "Significa"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "planned"
msgstr "planned"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Not yet shown"
msgstr "Aún no demostrada"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "met"
msgstr "met"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Shown, with evidence"
msgstr "Demostrada, con evidencias"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "deviation"
msgstr "deviation"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Will not be met; the consequence is recorded"
msgstr "No se cumplirá; la consecuencia queda registrada"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "not-applicable"
msgstr "not-applicable"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Does not apply, with the reason"
msgstr "No se aplica, con la razón"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Roles"
msgstr "Roles"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Documents name roles, never people."
msgstr "Los documentos nombran roles, nunca personas."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Role"
msgstr "Rol"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Responsible for"
msgstr "Responsable de"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Data Lead"
msgstr "Data Lead (responsable de datos)"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "What data is held and released; shares sign-off with the Technical Lead"
msgstr "Qué datos se conservan y se publican; comparte la aprobación con el Technical Lead"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Technical Lead"
msgstr "Technical Lead (responsable técnico)"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "How the platform is built and run; shares sign-off with the Data Lead"
msgstr "Cómo se construye y opera la plataforma; comparte la aprobación con el Data Lead"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Steward"
msgstr "Responsable de datos de un dominio (steward)"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "One domain's data, and who may see it"
msgstr "Los datos de un dominio y quién puede verlos"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Platform team"
msgstr "Equipo de plataforma"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Identity groups, shared infrastructure and the delivery pipeline"
msgstr "Los grupos de identidad, la infraestructura compartida y la cadena de entrega"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Operator"
msgstr "Operador"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Whoever carries out a procedure"
msgstr "Quien lleve a cabo un procedimiento"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "Domains and environments"
msgstr "Dominios y entornos"

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "A **domain** is an area of data with one steward, such as `learners` or `workforce`. Each is a catalog."
msgstr "Un **dominio** es un área de datos con una sola persona responsable, como `learners` o `workforce`. Cada uno es un catálogo."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "An **environment** is a separate world for a change to run in, such as production or a developer's branch. Catalogs are named `<domain>_<environment>`, for example `learners_prod`."
msgstr "Un **entorno** es un mundo separado en el que se ejecuta un cambio, como producción o la rama de un desarrollador. Los catálogos se llaman `<domain>_<environment>`, por ejemplo `learners_prod`."

#: docs/concepts/terminology.md
msgid "You are ready for the [specifications]{1}."
msgstr "Ya está preparado para las [especificaciones]{1}."
